   abstract = {This article presents two quantum algorithms for computing the product of a circulant matrix and a vector. The arithmetic complexity of the first algorithm is (Formula presented.) in most cases. For the second algorithm, when the entries in the circulant matrix and the vector take values in (Formula presented.) or (Formula presented.), the complexity is (Formula presented.) in most cases. However, when these entries take values from positive real numbers, the complexity is reduced to (Formula presented.) in most cases, which presents an exponential speedup compared to the classical complexity of (Formula presented.) for computing the product of a circulant matrix and vector. We apply this algorithm to the convolution calculation in quantum convolutional neural networks, which effectively accelerates the computation of convolutions. Additionally, we present a concrete quantum circuit structure for quantum convolutional neural networks. © 2024 by the authors.},
   author = {Lu Hou and Zhenyu Huang and Chang Lv},
